### Performance completion clarification

#125 is an optimization search, not permission to run a superficial baseline and retain the current implementation by default.

The completed lifecycle benchmark must isolate at least:

1. current gzip/object-per-file Drop;
2. zstd with dual-read compatibility;
3. hybrid zstd packfiles for small non-relocatable objects;
4. safe reflink/clonefile materialization where supported;
5. lazy/virtual materialization;
6. an immutable compressed filesystem-image representation with copy-on-write overlay where technically viable.

FUSE is a possible mechanism, not the architectural objective. OCI is evaluated separately as a carrier/index.

The final evidence must identify dominant publication/acquisition/materialization/startup costs and state:

- default storage encoding;
- default physical object layout;
- preferred Linux materializer;
- preferred macOS materializer;
- preferred Windows materializer;
- universal fallback;
- carrier recommendation.

Different platform/filesystem winners are allowed. Every candidate must preserve exact Artifact identity, relocation correctness, isolation, mutation safety, crash recovery, leases, verification, compatibility, and fallback.

If all named candidates miss the material-improvement gate, the work must profile the remaining dominant bottleneck, formulate at least one evidence-backed alternative, benchmark it when practical, and prove why the baseline remains optimal enough. No candidate is forced to win, and the search does not stop because the historical list was incomplete.
